  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>{{ site.legalName }} (company number <span class="data" translate="no">{{ site.companyNumber }}</span>), registered office {{ site.registeredOffice }}, is the controller responsible for your personal data. For any data protection question, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>We collect only what we need to run the business. Depending on how you deal with us, that may include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Contact details:</strong> name, company, email and phone number, from quote requests and correspondence.</li>
      <li><strong>Job applications:</strong> licence details, availability, right to work and anything you choose to tell us, including a CV if you send one.</li>
      <li><strong>Service details:</strong> site addresses, requirements and operational notes when clients engage us.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> standard server logs (such as IP address and browser type) kept by our hosting provider, GitHub, for security and performance.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How our forms work</h2>
    <p>The quote and application forms on this site do not send anything to a server. When you press the button, your own email app opens with your answers written into a message to us, and nothing is sent until you send that email. We then hold it like any other email we receive.</p>

    <h2>Why we use it (legal basis)</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>To answer enquiries and provide quotes:</strong> legitimate interest and, once engaged, performance of a contract.</li>
      <li><strong>To process job applications:</strong> legitimate interest in recruitment and, if we offer you a role, steps needed before entering a contract.</li>
      <li><strong>To deliver security services:</strong> performance of our contract with the client.</li>
      <li><strong>To meet legal and regulatory duties:</strong> SIA licensing, BS 7858 vetting, insurance and HMRC records.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal data. We share it only where needed to deliver our services, under suitable contracts: for example vetting agencies, our insurers, our auditors and our IT providers.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Enquiries:</strong> 12 months from last contact.</li>
      <li><strong>Unsuccessful job applications:</strong> 12 months, then deleted unless you ask us to keep them on file.</li>
      <li><strong>Employee and contractor records:</strong> the length of the engagement plus 6 years, as HMRC and regulatory rules require.</li>
      <li><strong>Client records:</strong> the length of the engagement plus 7 years, for accounting, insurance and audit.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct or delete it, restrict or object to how we use it, and ask for a portable copy. Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>. We will reply within one month.</p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies, storage and other services</h2>
    <p>This site uses no tracking or advertising cookies and no analytics. Our fonts and scripts are served from our own site.</p>
    <p><strong>Maps.</strong> Our maps are off until you allow them in the cookie prompt, or press “Show the map” and allow them there. Then your browser fetches map tiles from the <strong>OpenStreetMap Foundation</strong>, which can see your IP address, browser type and the map area requested. We do not receive those logs. The OpenStreetMap Foundation’s privacy policy is at <a href="https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy" rel="noopener">osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy</a>.</p>
    <p><strong>Remembering your choice.</strong> Your answer to the cookie prompt is stored in your browser’s local storage under the key <code>spike-consent-v1</code>, so you are not asked on every page. It holds no personal information. You can change it at any time.</p>
    <p class="js-only"><button type="button" class="btn btn--ghost btn--sm" data-consent-open>Change cookie settings</button></p>
    <p><strong>Links.</strong> The office map links to Google Maps for directions. If you follow it, Google’s privacy policy applies.</p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>We take reasonable technical and organisational steps to protect personal data against loss, unauthorised access and disclosure, including encrypted connections, access controls and staff training.</p>

    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>If you are unhappy with how we have handled your personal data, tell us so we can put it right. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a> or on <a class="data nb" translate="no" href="tel:+443031231113">0303 123 1113</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
    <p>We may update this notice from time to time. The version in force is the one on this page, and the date at the top shows when it was last reviewed.</p>
